<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="CIFS Datei-Explorer" pubkey="" timestamp="1792846689" url="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/quompacc/cifs-datei-explorer/fdroid/repo" version="20002"><description>Offizielles Repo von CIFS Datei-Explorer: SMB-Netzwerkfreigaben direkt in der Android-Dateien-App. Quellcode: https://github.com/quompacc/cifs-datei-explorer</description></repo><application id="de.cifsdateiexplorer"><id>de.cifsdateiexplorer</id><added>2026-10-24</added><lastupdated>2026-10-24</lastupdated><name>CIFS Datei-Explorer</name><summary>Network shares (SMB) directly in the Android Files app.</summary><desc>&lt;b&gt;CIFS Datei-Explorer&lt;/b&gt; adds your network shares – NAS, Windows PC, Samba server – directly to the Android Files app. No extra file manager needed: shares show up as a storage location in &quot;Files&quot; and in every file picker.

&lt;b&gt;Features&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SMB 2/3 (smbj, jCIFS-NG) and SMB 1, plus FTP, FTPS and SFTP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration via the Storage Access Framework (SAF) – works with every app that opens or saves files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stream videos and music directly from your NAS, including seeking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discover devices in your local network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple connections, reorderable via drag &amp;amp; drop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encrypted export/import of connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern Material 3 design with dynamic colors (Material You) and dark mode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully translated into German, more languages included&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The app itself is not a file manager – manage your files in the Files app or any other SAF-capable app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apps that only support local storage may not work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

Based on &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/wa2c/cifs-documents-provider&quot;&gt;CIFS Documents Provider&lt;/a&gt; by wa2c (MIT license).
